From 5990e3a271045d5e7d73cd0e8789195084f02ba9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r0ny123 <49360849+r0ny123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:08:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Let several workers run side by side

mcrit-worker carried container_name: mcrit-worker, and Docker allows one container per
name, so `docker compose up --scale mcrit-worker=2` refused ("Docker requires each
container to have a unique name. Remove the custom name to scale the service"). A worker
runs one job at a time, so that capped a deployment at one job at a time.

The fixed name is gone from both compose files, and deploy.replicas takes MCRIT_WORKERS,
default 1, so an unchanged .env starts exactly one worker as before. Running several is
safe: MCRIT's queue claims a job with one find_one_and_update that matches only an unset
locked_by and sets it, and every worker has its own uuid4 consumer id and releases only
its own jobs.

Checked with compose v5.1.1 and stand-in images for the worker and MongoDB: one worker
by default, two with MCRIT_WORKERS=2, three with --scale mcrit-worker=3, and
`docker compose config` accepts both files. The README says how to size and address the
workers; the changelog carries the container-name change under Upgrading.
